{"evidence":["Reviewed the checkpoint in a detached worktree at commit `c1440e7` to avoid unrelated moving workspace changes during review.","`cargo test --test cycling concentration_kinetics` passed in that detached worktree: both `concentration_kinetics_are_volume_independent` and `concentration_kinetics_volume_independent_extreme_scales` succeeded.","`crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:548` builds 10 L and 100 L states with matched TAN/NO2/DOC/DO concentrations, volume-proportional guild biomass, growth/decay zeroed, non-nitrogen couplings disabled, then asserts equal per-liter deltas for TAN/NO2/NO3/DOC/DON after one `step_nitrogen_cycle` tick.","`crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:632-680` also checks pre-tick Monod-style limitation factors from the normalized concentration parameters, and `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:753` repeats the rate-invariance check at 1 L vs 1000 L for the requested extreme-scale guardrail.","Inference from pre-refactor code inspection at commit `587dc4a`: `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:83-90` and `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:138-179` used total-mass terms (`do_total`, `doc_total`, `ammonia_total_mg_n_total`, `tan_after_aob`) directly in Monod calculations, so the new mg/L delta assertions target the historical tank-size artifact the bead describes.","Full-workspace validation for this historical checkpoint is not available as approval evidence because unchanged integration tests already fail to compile due missing `colonizable_area_factor` initializers (for example `crates/tank_core/tests/substrate_filter_integration.rs:35`), which is outside this diff."],"findings_or_gaps":["No task-specific correctness or completeness findings in the new cycling regression tests."],"follow_up_or_amendments":[],"outcome":"approved"}